<title>UK: UK govt confirms power stake sales.</title>
<headline>UK govt confirms power stake sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government on Tuesday confirmed it had sold its holdings in National Power and Southern Electric to Goldman Sachs and its holding in PowerGen to UBS for onward sale to institutional investors.</p>
<p>Just over 28 million National Power shares, 856,000 Southern Electric shares and 17 million PowerGen shares were sold.</p>
<p>The only shares retained by the government are to meet its obligations to pay bonus shares in respect of the sale of National Power and PowerGen shares in March 1995.</p>
<p>The sale took place following a competitive auction organised by Rothschilds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
